From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Palmer <dodava@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:28:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wm8962: Don't turn off SYSCLK that was already on

wm8962_configure_bclk() turns SYSCLK on to read back DSPCLK_DIV and off
again afterwards when the bias level isn't SND_SOC_BIAS_ON, assuming that
SYSCLK must have been off. But SYSCLK can be on below SND_SOC_BIAS_ON:
supply widgets only bring the context up to STANDBY, and
wm8962_mic_detect() force-enables the SYSCLK widget. At hw_params time
the provisional sequence then clears SYSCLK_ENA, while DAPM still
considers the widget powered and never sets it again. Playback runs
with SYSCLK stopped: the DC servo times out ("DC servo timed out") and
nothing comes out of the speakers or headphones.

Seen on the Microsoft Surface RT, whose Tegra machine driver uses
wm8962_mic_detect(). Only turn SYSCLK on and off again if it was off.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c
index ab8247ae431f..7e6c4c952e35 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8962.c
@@ -2474,6 +2474,7 @@ static void wm8962_configure_bclk(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	int clocking2 = 0;
 	int clocking4 = 0;
 	int aif2 = 0;
+	bool sysclk_off;
 
 	if (!wm8962->sysclk_rate) {
 		dev_dbg(component->dev, "No SYSCLK configured\n");
@@ -2505,9 +2506,13 @@ static void wm8962_configure_bclk(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 	/* DSPCLK_DIV can be only generated correctly after enabling SYSCLK.
 	 * So we here provisionally enable it and then disable it afterward
-	 * if current bias_level hasn't reached SND_SOC_BIAS_ON.
+	 * if it was off. Checking the bias level isn't enough: SYSCLK can be
+	 * on below SND_SOC_BIAS_ON, e.g. when microphone detection forces it,
+	 * and turning it off then would leave it off behind DAPM's back.
 	 */
-	if (snd_soc_component_get_bias_level(component) != SND_SOC_BIAS_ON)
+	sysclk_off = !(snd_soc_component_read(component, WM8962_CLOCKING2) &
+		       WM8962_SYSCLK_ENA);
+	if (sysclk_off)
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, WM8962_CLOCKING2,
 				WM8962_SYSCLK_ENA_MASK, WM8962_SYSCLK_ENA);
 
@@ -2521,7 +2526,7 @@ static void wm8962_configure_bclk(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	usleep_range(500, 1000);
 	dspclk = snd_soc_component_read(component, WM8962_CLOCKING1);
 
-	if (snd_soc_component_get_bias_level(component) != SND_SOC_BIAS_ON)
+	if (sysclk_off)
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, WM8962_CLOCKING2,
 				WM8962_SYSCLK_ENA_MASK, 0);
 
